      "textEn": "139\n\nOr if there is an influence of bad planets like Ketu, then he is not able to progress in any future work. On the contrary, Prahlada Maharaj was influenced by the supreme planet Krishna. Therefore, they could neither think about the physical world,\nnor could they live without Krishna consciousness. This is the characteristic of the great Bhagavata. Even if someone is an enemy of Krishna, the great devotee sees him also engaged in the service of Krishna.\n. Another classic example is jaundice where everything looks yellow to a person with jaundice. Similarly,\nMahabhagavat seems to be engaged in the service of Krishna, besides himself. Prahlad Maharaj is a certified Mahabhagavat, that is, a supreme devotee. It is said in the previous verse that\nthere was a natural attraction in them (Naisargiki Rati). In this verse, the characteristics of such natural love towards Krishna are described. Although Prahlad Maharaj was still a child, he had no interest in playing.\nAs it is said in\nSrimad Bhagavatam (11.2.42)—Viraktianyatra cha—the characteristic of complete Krishna consciousness is that\na man does not take any interest in all material activities. For a small child, it is impossible to give up playing.\nBut Prahlad Maharaj, being situated in excellent devotion, always remained absorbed in the Samadhi of Krishna's divine essence. Just as a materialist is always lost in the thoughts of material gain,\nin the same way, a great devotee like Prahlad Maharaj is always absorbed in the thoughts of Krishna. Asinah paritushnashnashyanah prapyabrunvavan. These are the ones who are initiated into the Govinda. 38. Meaning of the word:\n\nAasinah—sitting; Paritran—wandering; Ashanah—eating; Shayanah—sleeping; Prapiban—drinking; Bruvan—speaking; Na—not; Anusandhitte—\nKnowing; Etani—All these activities; Govinda—By God, those who awaken the senses; Parirambhitah—Being embraced\nHaving become. Prahlada Maharaj was always absorbed in Krishna's thoughts.\nThus, 