      "textEn": "157\n\nNo progress can be made.\"\n\nDirectly by the authority of all the scriptures,\n\nIt is also read and understood. But, O Lord, dear to him.\n\nI bow to the lotus feet of the Guru. “The guru should be respected as much as God is, because he is\nGod's most trusted servant. This has been accepted by all the scriptures, and all the scholars follow it. Therefore, I respectfully bow to the lotus feet of such a guru who is an authentic representative of Shri Hari (Krishna).” The servant of God remains engaged in the most secret service of God. This service\nFreezes all bound souls from the clutches of Maya, in which man thinks, \"This person is my enemy\nand this is my friend.\"” In reality, God is the friend of all beings, and all beings are\ndaily servants of God. Oneness is possible only through this knowledge, not through artificial thought that each of us is God\nor equivalent to God.\nThe real knowledge is that God is the supreme master and we are all his servants,\nTherefore, we are all at the same level (position). Prahlad Maharaj had already been taught this by his guru Narad, but even then Prahlad was surprised how a deluded being considers someone\nas their friend and someone as their enemy. Until a person clings to dualistic philosophy and considers someone a friend and someone an enemy,\nhe should understand himself in the noose of Maya. The Mayavadi philosopher also remains in illusion, because he\nconsiders all beings as God and considers them as one. No one is equivalent to God. A servant can never be equal to his master. According to Vaishnava philosophy, the Swami (Lord) is one, and the servant is also one, but there remains a difference between the Swami and the servant even in a liberated state. In a bonded state, we\nthink that some creatures are our friends and others are our enemies. In this way, we remain in a state of duality.\nBut in the state of liberation, God is in the form of the Lord, and all beings are one because they are servants of God."
